<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Julius Echter von Mespelbrunn</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1545">1545</a>–<a href="/years/1617">1617</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Julius Echter von Mespelbrunn was prince-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wurzburg">Würzburg</a> from 1573 to 1617. A leading figure of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/counter-reformation">Counter-Reformation</a>, he forced Protestants to convert or leave, refounded the University of Würzburg in 1582 and built the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juliusspital">Juliusspital</a> hospital. His reign also saw large witch trials in the prince-bishopric.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/julius-echter-von-mespelbrunn.jpg" alt="Julius Echter von Mespelbrunn" width="270" height="365" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Julius_Echter_1586.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
